17:["$","main",null,{"id":"top","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-ink/10 bg-surface/40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"href":"/operating-system","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-mute transition hover:text-accent","children":"← All chapters"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5","children":"Chapter 2"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-mute","children":["· ",15," min read · illustrated"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 font-hand text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl","children":"A Short History & the OS Zoo"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg text-mute","children":"How the cost of a computer shaped every OS idea we still use"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"Operating systems did not arrive fully formed. Almost every idea we now take for granted, running many programs at once, protecting one program from another, giving each user a fair slice of the machine, was invented to solve a very concrete problem of its day. And the biggest problem, for decades, was money: computers were staggeringly expensive, so the whole job of the OS was to make sure that precious hardware was never sitting idle."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"That single pressure explains a surprising amount. As hardware went from a million-dollar machine shared by a whole university, to a chip cheap enough to put in every home, to a battery-powered phone in your pocket, to a rented sliver of a server in a data centre, the priorities shifted, but the core techniques kept getting reused. The container you deploy to the cloud today is, at heart, the great-grandchild of a 1960s time-sharing system."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"This chapter is a guided tour of that story. We are not memorising dates for a quiz; we are watching each OS technique get born from the constraints of its era, so that when we study it in depth later, you already know why it exists and what it was trying to fix."}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"sticky top-8 hidden h-fit w-56 shrink-0 lg:block","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-hand text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"On this page"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm","children":[["$","li","01-why-history-helps",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#01-why-history-helps","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"01"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"Why the history is worth your time"}]]}]}],["$","li","02-batch-era",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#02-batch-era","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"02"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"The batch era & the birth of the OS"}]]}]}],["$","li","03-multiprogramming-timesharing",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#03-multiprogramming-timesharing","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"03"}],"$L21"]}]}],"$L22","$L23","$L24"]}]]}],"$L25"]}],"$L26"]}]
